      "A good warm-up isn't about flexibility — it's about rehearsing the specific movement you're about to do and ramping up the load gradually, so your first work set of the day isn't also your heaviest set cold. Most lifters either skip this entirely or do the wrong kind of warm-up, and both mistakes cost performance in slightly different ways.",
